  "summary": "EtherRAT and TONResolver are NodeJS-based malware families delivered via malicious LNK shortcuts masquerading as JPG images in email campaigns targeting the hotel/accommodation industry. Instead of hardcoded C2, both resolve their current C2 address at runtime by reading data stored in Ethereum (EtherRAT) or TON (TONResolver) blockchain smart contracts via public APIs, enabling cheap C2 rotation and resisting takedown. Detection should focus on blockchain JSON-RPC/API lookups (eth_call), NodeJS runtime execution spawned by image-like LNK files, and the blockchain-derived C2 domains listed here.",
